Subject: [PATCH] meson: optionally link kmod tools statically

Keep the shared libkmod target available. Only the target executable uses
-static when explicitly requested, so host-kmod keeps its normal linking.
Combine with prefer_static=true and dlopen=[] to link compression directly.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Polis linking policy]

--- a/meson_options.txt
+++ b/meson_options.txt
@@ -112,3 +112,10 @@
   value : false,
   description : 'Build the documentation. Default: false',
 )
+
+option(
+  'static-tools',
+  type : 'boolean',
+  value : false,
+  description : 'Link the kmod executable statically',
+)
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -468,6 +468,7 @@
 kmod = executable(
   'kmod',
   kmod_sources,
+  link_args : get_option('static-tools') ? ['-static'] : [],
   link_with : [libshared, libkmod_internal],
   gnu_symbol_visibility : 'hidden',
   build_by_default : get_option('tools'),
